+````markdown name=services/serving/vllm_production_notes.md
+```text
+vLLM / Triton production notes (brief)
+
+- Use model repository pattern (/models/<model>/1) and cosign-sign model artifacts as part of CI.
+- For vLLM:
+  - Deploy on GPU nodes with large memory (e.g., A100/80GB).
+  - Use sharding & quantization where appropriate.
+  - Tune batch sizes and token limits; integrate warm-pool manager to reduce cold starts.
+- For Triton:
+  - Use ONNX or TorchScript model artifacts produced by training pipelines.
+  - Expose metrics and use Prometheus scraping.
+  - Use model control mode to hot-swap models and limit memory usage.
+
+Security:
+- Validate model signatures with cosign at deploy time and load only signed models.
+- Use admission controller to block unsigned model repository changes.
+````
